  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1249 PM CDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\nTonight \n\nHigh pressure will provide light winds and mostly clear skies\ntonight. This will allow temperatures to cool more than the past\nseveral nights. Due to this, lowered the low temperatures in\ncentral and north-central Wisconsin to the NBM 10th percentile.\nThese temperatures were in the 30s. This will result in patchy \nto scattered frost. This was far too little to issue a Frost \nAdvisory.\n\nWednesday into Wednesday Night \n\nHigh pressure over the Great Lakes will keep the Driftless\nRegion dry. High temperatures will be in the lower to mid-60s.\nLow temperatures will range from the mid-30s to around 50. The\ncoldest temperatures will be in central and north-central\nWisconsin.\n\nThursday afternoon into Thursday night\n\nA cold front will approach the Driftless Region from the\nNorthern Plains. This may result in a chance (20-50 percent) of\nshowers west of Highway 52 in northeast Iowa and southeast\nMinnesota. High temperatures will be in the lower and mid-60s.\nLow temperatures will range from the mid-40s to lower 50s.\n\nFriday into the Weekend\n\nThe 500 mb ridge will shift east of the area. This will allow a\nshortwave trough to move into the Driftless Region. As this\noccurs, there will be periodic showers and maybe a few storms.\nHigh temperatures will be in the 60s and low temperatures will \nrange from the mid-40s to mid-50s.",
